  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3f0d0e153d21a764da1ca6e6ba5afa2a, type: 3}
  m_Name: KidsHouseInfo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  houseType: 3
  menuTitle: School-Age Children
  choices:
  - choiceName: Wait for Notice
    carNumberMod: 0
    horseNumberMod: 0
    kidNumberMod: 0
    petNumberMod: 0
    homeHardeningMod: 0
    carSpeedMod: 2
    carLeaveTime: 2
    choiceDetail: 'No city-wide plan requests. Let residents make a decision when
      the evacuation notice goes out. '
    endGameFeedback: Families with children were unprepared for an evening evacuation,
      and there was a lot of confusion
    isLocked: 0
    isNormal: 1
  - choiceName: Pick up children
    carNumberMod: 0
    horseNumberMod: 0
    kidNumberMod: 2
    petNumberMod: 0
    homeHardeningMod: 0
    carSpeedMod: 0
    carLeaveTime: 1
    choiceDetail: Need Detail
    endGameFeedback: Families with children rushed to the school, which added unnecessary
      congestion in that area. Families are reminded that the school is one of the
      safest places in our community.
    isLocked: 0
    isNormal: 1
  - choiceName: Safer at school
    carNumberMod: 0
    horseNumberMod: 0
    kidNumberMod: 0
    petNumberMod: 0
    homeHardeningMod: 0
    carSpeedMod: 2
    carLeaveTime: 1
    choiceDetail: 'You know the children are safter at school  and have a plan that
      they know: they will stay  at school untill it is safe to pick them up.'
    endGameFeedback: Children sheltered at the school and were safe there. Thankfully
      families knew to evacuate first and wait until it was safe to go to the school
      to pick up the kids.
    isLocked: 1
    isNormal: 0
  longerTitle: School-Age Children
  descriptions:
  - Families with children have additional responsibilities to juggle during an evacuation.
    It is very important to make plans in advance and consider multiple scenarios
    and consequences of choices. Some parents choose to pick up their children from
    school when the evacuation notice goes out. However, this causes additional congestion
    around the school. Schools tend to be extremely safe places to shelter during
    an emergency. Parents should consider leaving the children at the school and
    waiting until it is safe to pick them up.
  carNumber: 1
  horseNumber: 0
  petNumber: 0
  kidNumber: 0
  carSpeed: 1
